    <md:uuid>ab28d3fd-87fa-476a-9072-0c6f3f2ea365</md:uuid>
  </metadata>
  <content>
  <section><para>Complete the following questions to practice the skills you have learned in this lesson.</para>
<section class="check-understanding"><exercise data-content-id="d746e47d-1480-40ae-a4c4-5f0f9911c402"><problem><para>
      <para> What is the slope of the line that goes through the points in the given table of values?</para>
      <table class="os-raise-horizontaltable">
        <thead>
        </thead>
        <tbody>
          <row>
            <entry><emphasis>\(x\)</emphasis></entry><entry>1</entry>
            <entry>2</entry>
            <entry>3</entry>
            <entry>4</entry>
          </row>
          <row>
            <entry><emphasis>\(y\)</emphasis></entry><entry>6</entry>
            <entry>11</entry>
            <entry>16</entry>
            <entry>21</entry>
          </row>
        </tbody>
      </table>
      
      <para>Enter your answer here.</para>
    </para></problem><solution><para>5</para><para>
      <para>The correct answer is 5. You seem to be stuck. Who can you ask for help?
      </para>
    </para></solution></exercise></section></section>
</content>
</document>
